<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>io.github.bluemesh_app.BlueMesh</id>
  <name>BlueMesh</name>
  <summary>Off-grid Bluetooth mesh chat for nearby devices</summary>

  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>MIT</project_license>

  <description>
    <p>
      BlueMesh is an off-grid chat app for Linux. It talks to nearby devices
      over a Bluetooth Low Energy mesh, so no internet connection, account or
      phone number is needed for mesh chat. It speaks the open BitChat mesh wire
      protocol and can chat with BitChat-compatible devices nearby.
    </p>
    <p>Features include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Public mesh chat with people in range</li>
      <li>End-to-end encrypted direct messages (Noise XX)</li>
      <li>Private file transfer to accepted contacts, with image preview</li>
      <li>Favourites, block list and emergency wipe</li>
      <li>Optional geohash location channels carried over Nostr relays</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Location channels use the internet and are public. Bluetooth mesh chat
      itself works without internet access.
    </p>
  </description>

  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.github.bluemesh_app.BlueMesh.desktop</launchable>

  <!-- TODO: replace with the real project GitHub URLs. -->
